  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nre: [Section 2.3.2\n](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#boolean-attributes)\nThe spec reads as follows:\n\n> \"If the attribute is present, its value must either be the empty string or a value that is an [ASCII case-insensitive](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive) match for the attribute's canonical name, with no leading or trailing whitespace.\"\n\nBut the first and third examples show usage where that \"must\" is not satisified:\ne.g. for  `<label><input type=checkbox checked name=cheese disabled> Cheese</label>`\n\n`checked` is present, but its value does not conform to the \"must\" statement in the spec.\n\nA suggested correction might be to either amend it to: \"If the attribute is present _and has a value_, its value must either...\" or to remove that section altogether (which would make 1 and 3 conform with the language present and is likely more germane to common practice). \n\n",
